    turnFlow: '1. Deal: Five cards each, counter-clockwise; one card turned up (wild indicator). Dealer stacks remainder as stock.\n2. Play: Dealer draws one from stock (has six cards), discards one face up in front of the player to his right. Each turn: take either the top card of the stock or the top discard in front of you (the card just discarded by the previous player), then discard one face up in front of the next player. Only the most recent discard in front of you is available.\n3. Winning: As soon as a player has six cards in hand forming three valid pairs, they win the deal. Pairs are: two cards totalling 10, two 10s, two Jacks, two Queens, or two Kings. Wild cards (three jokers plus three cards of the turned-up rank) can complete any pair.',
